{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5451) from a cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd068 R3.1-R3.4 for `cmd/csplit` — specifically the output control and prefix options for the csplit utility. The four requirements are:\n   - R3.1: Default output files named xx00, xx01, xx02, etc. (partially exists already in hardcoded form)\n   - R3.2: `-f PREFIX` or `--prefix=PREFIX` to customize output filename prefix\n   - R3.3: `-n DIGITS` or `--digits=DIGITS` to control numeric suffix width (default 2)\n   - R3.4: `-z` or `--elide-empty-files` to suppress creation of empty output files\n   \n   Acceptance criteria require: `go build` succeeds, `go vet` passes, `go test` passes (with gcsplit differential testing), and all SRD R3.1-R3.4 acceptance criteria are met.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU csplit utility reimplementation in Go\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew `gcsplit` reference binary via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Pattern-based file splitting (regex, line numbers, skip patterns, repeat counts)\n   - Command-line flag parsing (currently manual, no cobra/flag)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys`\n   - The cobbler-scaffold pipeline (measure + stitch phases)\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd068-csplit.yaml**\n     - Full SRD specification for csplit with R1-R4 requirement groups\n     - R3.1-R3.4 are the target requirements for this task\n     - Acceptance criteria AC3 specifically tests `-f chunk -n 3` with `{*}` repeat\n     - Non-goals: no `--suppress-matched` beyond basic, no `--keep-files`\n   \n   - **cmd/csplit/main